From 7c0b09492aeec57b122bab5e612b18dc871f606b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Desktop: drive fetchJson/fetchPublicJson themselves
 in tests (json-fetch.ts seam)

PR #1981 review nit: api-transport.test.ts proves sendWithRequestDeadline,
but nothing failed if fetchJson or fetchPublicJson stopped calling it (an
inline req.write + deadline.arm(req, reject) without the body size).

Move both helpers out of main.ts into electron/json-fetch.ts
(fetchJsonWith / fetchPublicJsonWith) with main.ts's remote-header and
native-grant sources passed in as deps; main.ts keeps thin fetchJson /
fetchPublicJson wrappers, so every caller is unchanged.

json-fetch.test.ts drives both against a live loopback server:
- a ~125 KB POST to a server busy 600 ms answers under a 200 ms timeout
  (body-scaled budget), and a small body times out at exactly its budget;
- a POST dropped after the server read it is not replayed (bodySent),
  while a dropped GET is retried;
- pool: 'probe' rides the 2-socket probe pool (a third probe queues),
  replacing the main.ts source regex for it in remote-down-gate.test.ts.

RED: fetchJson with inline write/arm and no body size fails the two budget
tests; arm with the body but no bodySent fails the replay test; ignoring
options.pool fails the probe-pool test.
